(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #111. Reading a nested collection OUT - `element N of
 <list>` - hands back a copy; the parent's own slot is untouched by a
 later write to the copy.)

a list called inner is [1, 2].
a list called outer is [inner, 3].
a list called got is element 1 of outer.
Set element 1 of got to 555.
print outer.
print got.
